      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Domestic expansion",
          "heading": "FRU chairman John Sanday says Solomon Islands want into Fiji domestic competitions",
          "body": "Fiji's domestic club rugby is drawing regional suitors. Sanday told the Fiji Sun that Solomon Islands are \"excited about the idea\" and talks are planned when their Usotasi club visits for the Nadi junior tournament in early December. A Tonga official raised the idea at the Skipper Cup final, France has pitched Wallis & Futuna, New Caledonia and Tahiti, and three Papua New Guinea unions, frustrated by PNG's World Rugby suspension, asked to join FRU."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 in Nations Championship",
          "body": "Scotland beat Japan 67-5. France's Philippe Sella wins Jauréguy-Dominici prize. Former Ireland U20 Noah Byrne joins AFL's Brisbane Lions."
        }
      ]
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-25",
      "edition": "Wednesday 25 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Haka row",
          "heading": "England risk fine for drafting Lewis Moody to face All Blacks' haka",
          "body": "The Sun reports that England's decision to bring Rugby World Cup winner Moody in to face New Zealand's haka could cost them a fine. Today's press does not say who would impose it or how much it might be. The row comes before Saturday's rematch at Allianz Stadium, where England meet the All Blacks for third place in the Nations Championship finals weekend. Borthwick's side won the Round 6 meeting 37-12, which Matt Dawson's BBC column called a record win for a northern hemisphere side over New Zealand."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland beat Japan 67-5",
          "body": "France's Philippe Sella wins Jauréguy-Dominici prize. Former Ireland U20 Noah Byrne joins AFL's Brisbane Lions."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Allianz Stadium, Twickenham"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-25",
      "edition": "Wednesday 25 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Legend honoured",
          "heading": "Philippe Sella edges Jean-Pierre Rives to win the Jauréguy-Dominici prize",
          "body": "France's 111-cap centre was chosen in Paris on Tuesday by a jury of journalists, former players and rugby figures, and the vote was tight between him and Jean-Pierre Rives. The ceremony fell on the anniversary of Christophe Dominici's death. The prize was created in 1980 to honour Franco-British rugby ties. It lapsed after 1997 and was revived two years ago with a wider brief. Sella fits the original purpose: he was the first French player in the English league, with Saracens from 1996 to 1998."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England beat All Blacks 37-12 in Nations Championship",
          "body": "Scotland beat Japan 67-5. Former Ireland U20 Noah Byrne joins AFL's Brisbane Lions."
