          "heading": "Taine Randell blames loose forwards after England beat All Blacks 37-12",
          "body": "Former All Blacks captain Taine Randell told The Platform NZ podcast he was \"zero percent confident that we were going to get absolutely smoked\" at Twickenham, which is exactly what England then did. The ex-back-row, who played 51 Tests between 1997 and 2002, said New Zealand's loose forwards no longer win the collision: \"we just do not dominate the advantage line.\" He also pointed to what he calls \"an obsession\" in New Zealand with a flashy style of play, especially at Super Rugby level."
